$\begin{align}
&\phantom{=}\dfrac{x^4+2x^3-3x^2}{x^3-x^2}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{x^2(x-1)(x+3)}{x^2(x-1)}\qquad\gray{\text{Factor numerator & denominator}}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{\cancel {x^2}\cancel{(x-1)}(x+3)}{\cancel {x^2}\cancel{(x-1)}}\qquad\gray{\text{Cancel out common factors}}
\\\\
&=x+3, \text{ for }x\neq 0,1
\end{align}$
